hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27572","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Haram, that she said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was taking midday rest in my house, he woke laughing. I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, what makes you laugh? He said: People of my nation were displayed to me riding the back of this sea like kings upon thrones. I said: Supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: O Allah, make her among them. Then he slept again and woke laughing. I said: May my father and mother be ransom, what makes you laugh? He said: People of my nation were displayed to me riding this sea like kings upon thrones. I said: Supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: You are among the first. She campaigned with Ubadah ibn al-Samit, and he was her husband, and a gray mule of hers threw her, and she fell and died."
"27573","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed me, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Haram, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke in my house, and he mentioned its meaning."
"27921","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, from Umm Haram bint Milhan, she being his maternal aunt, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slept, or he said: in her house, and awoke laughing. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what makes you laugh. He said: People of my nation were shown to me, riding the back of this green sea, like kings upon thrones. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: You are among them. Then he slept and awoke laughing. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what made you laugh. He said: People of my nation were shown to me, riding the back of this green sea, like kings upon thrones. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: You are among the first. He said: Then Ubadah ibn al-Samit married her and took her out with him, and when he crossed the sea with her, she rode a beast and it threw her and killed her."
"27922","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Umm Haram bint Milhan narrated to me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, napped in her house one day, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, awoke laughing, then he mentioned its meaning."
